<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAFRICA MONEY MKT SHORTAGE GROWS TO 9.697 BLN RAND.</title>
<headline>SAFRICA MONEY MKT SHORTAGE GROWS TO 9.697 BLN RAND.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage grew to 9.697 billion rand on Tuesday from 9.064 billion rand on Monday, the Reserve Bank said.  </p>
<p>Banks quoted their three-month NCD rates unchanged at between 16.90 percent and 17.00 percent offered and 17.10 and 17.20 percent offered, while the 90-day BA rate was also unmoved at between 16.30 and 16.60 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
